{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475582-twists-of-fate","id":1475582,"title":"Twists of Fate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-28T10:26:34-08:00","id":1475582,"title":"Twists of Fate","content":"The Fate Arcanum is a flexible tool, providing mages a broad array of potential effects in exchange for some of the control the Awakened are used to: Casting a Life spell to injure someone places a Supernal symbol for harm right onto the victim\u2019s body, while using Fate as a weapon could cause the target to slip on ice, find a coral snake in their mailbox, or suffer a sudden aneurysm. Even more troubling, compared to the other Arcana, Fate spells are more likely to continue affecting the world even after the original magic expires: Nudge your destiny to choose a winning lottery ticket, and the person who was originally meant to win the jackpot never strikes it rich, meaning they never buy that condo in the city\u2019s new upscale neighborhood, meaning they never come into contact with the strange entity that haunts the building\u2019s elevator and which ultimately would have led to their Awakening. The world comprises nigh-innumerable moving pieces, intricately interlocked, many invisible or at least subtle in their affect, and an incautious student of Arcadia may find their Wisdom fraying from the strain of all the wanton eddies let loose into reality. Every choice begets new consequences, after all, each of which demands a new choice to be made in turn.<br /> <br /> Mages commonly call the unforeseen side-effects of casting Fate spells Twists. They are grounded in the natural causality of the world, and thus aren\u2019t Paradox Anomalies, nor are they the same category of Imago-error arising from the Hitches of warped rotes. A Twist can be accounted for and mitigated, sometimes with additional magic, other times by chasing down loose ends that arise from things being jarred out of place, and often just by taking things slow and steady, following the maxim of that one group of aliens in that one Animorphs spin-off book. I forget which one, there were a lot of those things. The one where the plot gets horrific and weird by the end.<br /> <br /> The system for Twists comes into play when a mage casts a spell using the Fate Arcanum whose effect relies on manipulating the unseen levers of the world. Knowing and Unveiling spells are generally excluded (with the exception of unique situations like the specific Reach effects of Serendipity), as are any effects that are immediate and confined in both time and space. Example spells where Twists are appropriate include Reading the Outermost Eddies, Exceptional Luck, Strings of Fate, and Miracle. After a successful casting, the Storyteller rolls a number of dice equal to the spell\u2019s required Fate rating (so, for instance, four dice for Chaos Mastery). Subtract one die for each dot of Fate the mage possesses over the required rating for the spell, and add one die for every unsafe Reach included in the casting. Add two more dice if Advanced Duration is employed, and subtract one more die for each ritual interval the mage takes when casting the spell (in addition to the normal spellcasting bonus from such). Legacy Attainments never provoke Twists, while Imbued Items and Artifacts compare their in-built Fate rating against the spell for determining the dice pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The spell provokes a minor Twist, causing an unexpected problem in the weave of Fate. This might take the form of a dice penalty equal to the spell\u2019s dot rating at some point later in the story to an appropriate action, a moderate or temporary Condition, or a side-effect whose consequences would trigger an Act of Hubris against Enlightened Wisdom. If the Twist causes an appreciable setback to the caster or their cabal, they gain a Beat (normal or Arcane, their choice).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The spell provokes a major Twist. The caster or someone with whom they share ties might automatically fail an appropriate roll, lose access to a Merit for the rest of the story, suffer a grave or persistent Condition, or be faced with an Act of Hubris against Understanding Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>Either no Twist occurs, or any Twist that does arise is as trivial as a light breeze on a warm springtime afternoon.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> It turns out that the mage\u2019s casting of the spell, and any natural consequence arising from it, was already encoded into Fate\u2019s designs. The caster takes an Arcane Beat. This may also present the opportunity for a new Mystery to explore.<br /> <br /> Because they\u2019re the result of so many variable factors often spread across wide distances, Twists can\u2019t be divined ahead of time or mystically altered without the Imperial Practices. A Fate Knowing spell cast on the subject of a spell will reveal whether there is a Twist attached to it, and a Time Knowing spell will reveal what form it will most likely take. An informed willworker can take pains to prevent, soften, or reroute a Twist (and some Consilia expect this of members who carelessly snap the loom of destiny), though do keep in mind what tends to happen when you try to plug holes in dams with your fingers.<br /> <br /> <b>On Using Twists</b><br /> <br /> The Twist system is ultimately meant to represent a give-and-take between a mage and Fate. It arises from the particularities of the Fate Arcanum, but is not meant to punish players for wanting to cast spells they\u2019ve invested Experiences into casting. As with Paradox, effective use of Twists requires a degree of communication and trust between player and Storyteller, and the best Twists are those which either facilitate new and interesting story hooks, or which play into Awakening\u2019s themes of power and hubris. A mage casts Strings of Fate to gain access to a certain Grimoire, but it arrives in her hands through theft from an Atheneum, and now a Mystagogue investigator is searching for it. An Initiate of Fate overreaches on Serendipity to punk-rock his way into a top secret government lab, only to find that the scientists have been expecting him all along. Paranoid Libertines and devout Seers look for signs of the Ruin in the vagaries stirred up in the wake of powerful magics, while Banishers exploit their existence to fuel their rhetoric against the Awakened as irresponsible meddlers in affairs they have no hope of understanding.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Prelacy</b><br /> <br /> The Ruin grants his favored servitors the Crown of Punishment: Whenever the Seer observes a mage casting a spell through Active Mage Sight, she may spend a point of Mana and roll Gnosis + Fate contested by the caster\u2019s Gnosis + Arcanum. On a success, she imposes a minor Twist on the spell, which becomes a major Twist on an exceptional success. The Prelate does not have control over how the Twist manifests, but this can be used even against spells outside the Fate Arcanum so long as they have an effect on the world that could potentially beget further consequences.<br /> <br /> <b>Butterfly\u2019s Gale (Fate 3)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> One Mana<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Computer, Drive, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> This spell alters a mage\u2019s imbuement process, creating an Item whose magic is prone to unforeseen consequences. Any appropriate Fate spells cast by the Item add this spell\u2019s Potency to the dice pool for their potential Twists.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach, Add Arcanum 1:</b> Appropriate spells that fall under the included Arcanum the Item casts also risk Twists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T11:21:20-08:00","id":1475583,"title":"","content":"I feel like this could be really interesting, but as you said, it requires careful balancing so the player does not feel cheated: &quot;So if we had just waltzed in with Forces invisibility we would be fine, but using luck means we default on getting preempted ? Why ?&quot; Its a difficult balancing act.<br /> <br /> In addition, I think a natural development of this would be an Unveiling effect to determine cosmic cost. In other words, an action that would counterbalance the scales. This way Fate would be more likely to make sure there is progress towards a better overall state of affairs. We have an NPC that works like in a campaign I am in, his Blue and Orange morality scares and confuses us. It has been overall beneficial, but requires very careful consideration before accepting his deals.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Prelacy, I think the effect is interesting, but the name might be a bit off. A Crown effect is named after recognizing what the Exarch does and then accepting their blessing to rule over the Fallen. The Prophet chains those not chosen to a single destiny, but you tell them all where to march, for only you have Agency. The General inflicts violence and suffering through dehumanizing war, let your foes beware your Fury. The Eye sees all and knows all, no one can oppose you if they cannot escape your unerring Vision. <br /> <br /> With this in mind, the Ruin is about entropy, everything ends up falling apart and breaking in the end. I think calling it the Prelacy of Triumph would follow the overall style. <br /> <br /> But ultimately, I think this concept would make for a fascinating Legacy of rebalancers of Fate. Maybe with mixed Prime, so they could always perceive the truth, grant knowledge of what lead to a target's karmic status and if they are in debt, receive detailed revelations on what these balancing acts would do and allow the to craft imbued items that could be &quot;purchased&quot; (safely relinquished) by the completion of such a task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T13:24:09-08:00","id":1475588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475582-twists-of-fate?p=1475583#post1475583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this could be really interesting, but as you said, it requires careful balancing so the player does not feel cheated: &quot;So if we had just waltzed in with Forces invisibility we would be fine, but using luck means we default on getting preempted ? Why ?&quot; Its a difficult balancing act.</div> </div> </div> </div>My hope with the system is that the potential for extra Beats compensates for the potential complications. The Storyteller should definitely refrain from using Twists to cheat players out of the desired effects of the spell, but rather to make things more interesting or with a thematic catch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In terms of the Prelacy, I think the effect is interesting, but the name might be a bit off. A Crown effect is named after recognizing what the Exarch does and then accepting their blessing to rule over the Fallen. The Prophet chains those not chosen to a single destiny, but you tell them all where to march, for only you have Agency. The General inflicts violence and suffering through dehumanizing war, let your foes beware your Fury. The Eye sees all and knows all, no one can oppose you if they cannot escape your unerring Vision.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, the Ruin is about entropy, everything ends up falling apart and breaking in the end. I think calling it the Prelacy of Triumph would follow the overall style. </div> </div> </div>You know, I never could quite divine the logic behind the names of Crowns. That's sensible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But ultimately, I think this concept would make for a fascinating Legacy of rebalancers of Fate. Maybe with mixed Prime, so they could always perceive the truth, grant knowledge of what lead to a target's karmic status and if they are in debt, receive detailed revelations on what these balancing acts would do and allow the to craft imbued items that could be &quot;purchased&quot; (safely relinquished) by the completion of such a task. </div> </div> </div>As I was finalizing the mechanics, I started to wonder if there were the seeds of a Legacy buried somewhere in this. Maybe mages who take up the Daoine's schtick but for internal affairs, tracking down the ripples other Awakened spread with their magic, cleaning up messes and punishing those who continuously overreach, Guardians of the Veil par excellence.<br /> <br /> Also, it could make for an interesting Fate Utility Attainment: Maybe something like increase the Primary Factor of a Fate spell by one step in exchange for automatically generating a Twist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T15:37:04-08:00","id":1475601,"title":"","content":"Some Thread Cutters could engage with this (even without using the mechanics itself). Tying up the unexpectedly literal loose ends of Fate, and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}